[b]Speculative Markets 1.1.6[/b]

[list]
[*]On the Speculation tab, click Risk to rank goods by their projected loss of Market Confidence. Hover over a number to see the calculation, including peak interest, type of crash, market share, bank exposure, supply growth and market conditions. The existing category, interest and intervention filters work with the sort.
[*]Pressures and Risks display one decimal place. Pressure tooltips retain their finer breakdown. Investor Interest chart shares now add up to 100.0% when there is trade, and each slice keeps the correct interest level between monthly updates.
[*]Banking separates each good’s share of boom loans from its share of all credit. Hover over Other Goods to see its three largest contributors. An empty chart explains current lending conditions.
[*]Panic tooltips record the outstanding balance, requested recall and investment-pool limit. A failed rescue pledge explains the cause, any reserve shortfall and whether the pledge still stands.
[*]Recovering goods show their return date and days remaining. Great Issue tooltips show when the issue ends and when another can begin. Company tooltips show separate expiry dates for Propped Up and Fragile.
[*]Charter previews show the trust change and which specialities a switch would cost. Our Last Move records the rival, treasury cost and duration of Shore Up.
[/list]

On an existing save, the Investor Interest chart refreshes at the next monthly update. New panics, recoveries and company effects record their additional details as they happen.
